    "source": "BodyParts3D 4.0, PART-OF tree, 99% polygon reduction (dbarchive.biosciencedbc.jp)",
    "recipe": "apps/worker3d/library/recipes/heart.json",
    "rawTriangles": 195208,
    "notes": [
      "BodyParts3D 4.0 has no ventricular wall (myocardium) mesh: the ventricles are casts of their cavities, the atria have walls.",
      "Pulmonary arteries and veins keep only their main trunks near the heart (branches inside the lungs are left out); the inferior vena cava is clipped to the heart's neighbourhood.",
      "Ventricular walls are RECONSTRUCTED, not scanned: BodyParts3D has only the ventricle cavities, so each cavity was grown by a typical wall thickness (left 8 mm, right 3 mm, within normal adult ranges and chosen so the coronary arteries lie on the surface) and the walls fused into a septum. The ventricles' outer shape is an approximation."
    ]
  }
